    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31969" root="غضر" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضِرٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضِيرٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  One says also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْشٌ غَضِرٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَضِرٌ</span> <i>An easy and a plentiful life:</i> (K, * TA:)
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مضر</span> being here an imitative sequent to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عضر</span>.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضِرُ النَّاصِيَةِ</span> applied to a man,
(O, K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضِرَةُ النَّاصِيَةِ</span> applied to a beast
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَّابَّة</span>), (O, Msb, K,) <i>Blest, fortunate,</i> or <i>abounding in good</i> or <i>advantage</i> or <i>utility.</i> (O, Msb, K.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَضْرَآءُ</span>, in two places.

